extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 3: England printed 22-25 (cache p023-p026, cache page = printed folio + 1). Printed 22 is welded in the cache and printed 24 digit-substituted; the O.C.C. block and skill list were read off a render of printed 24, the powers off the cache checked against the renders. The entry starts at the Herbalist O.C.C. heading on printed 22 and ends at Cybernetics & Bionics on printed 25, above the Herbs heading. || GROUP: under The Herbalists, Druids, Herbs, & Magic (printed 22); the book calls the herbalist a mage, sorcerer and practitioner of magic with a P.P.E. base and P.P.E.-costed powers, so occ_group is magic; it states no S.D.C. base, so men_of_arms is false. || XP: the column headed Herbalist, Woodland Druids, Blood Druids on the Experience Tables, printed 152 (cache p153), read off a render; every low bound is the previous high plus one. || POOLS: hit points not printed; P.E. + 1D6 per level as for the book''s other O.C.C.s. P.P.E. 2D4x10 + P.E., +1D6 per additional level. || BONUSES: +2 vs mind control (psionic or chemical), +2 vs poison (toxins_poisons), +2 vs horror factor. || POWERS: the six O.C.C. Powers and ten Special Magic Powers are stored as special abilities, every one granted; the three percentage powers carry their base in the description. Power 5 (bonuses) is applied; power 6 is the Mystic Herbology skill. The P.P.E. costs are prose, as no catalog spell rows exist for them. || SKILLS: each base is the catalog base plus the printed bonus. Mystic Herbology is the row of printed 22 (+15%). Identify Plants & Fruits is the catalog Identify Plants & Fruit. English has no language or literacy row, so it rides Language: Other at the printed figure and a one-pick Literacy: Other group at +20% (row ruling, 2026-11-12: no language skill rows). The +10% to the horsemanship skill is stored as a Horsemanship category bonus beside the Pilot +5%. Hand to Hand Basic may become Expert for one other skill: costs { expert: 1 }. || EQUIPMENT: 15 magic herb items of choice, from the held herb-* rows less the wands, staves, throwing stick and mandrake doll (the page names magic food, dried fruit, bark, leaves, potions and ointments, and the herbalist cannot make wands); the herbs of legend are not offered. Not stored: the 1D4x10+5 non-magical herbs, scissors, plant snippers, a box of 50 small plastic bags, and magical bark or leaf armor (traditional, not issued). Tent or sleeping bag is stored as the sleeping bag; rope or cord as nylon cord; several knives as three."
---

# Herbalist

## Lore

An herbalist is a native of Rifts England, Scotland or Ireland, male or female, human, elf or D-bee, attuned to plant life beyond most druids. A childhood diet of mutant mushrooms, eaten weekly for at least the first ten years of life, carries microbes that change the body over years; the mutation ties the herbalist to the land and lets him channel ley line energy into plants. He identifies alien species, grows a tree from sapling to adult in minutes, becomes a tree, and instills ordinary herbs with magic. His most sought after gift is the brewing of powerful teas and potions.

## GM Notes

Herbalists and druids are careful about selling mystic herbs, and cruel kings, knights, warriors and monsters are known to capture herbalists and force them to make potions. Payment for healing ranges from a bowl of soup to thousands of credits; most herbalists are selfish and mercenary, keeping the best for themselves. Starting kit beyond the sheet: 1D4x10+5 non-magical herbs, scissors, plant snippers and a box of 50 small plastic bags. Many wear magical bark or leaf armor from the Millennium tree or light synthetic armor. Most like horses, bionic horses and hovercycles.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'herbalist');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'herbalist';

